@nsobid-FF1D1C05670DB6021C85B624A710B963

# Animal Crossing: New Horizons 3.0.3 - 4096x4096 depth shadow map

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Forces the sun cascade shadow map to 4096x4096 so shadow edges stop
// being blocky.
//
// The game writes the shadow size into gsys's depth_shadow_tex_width /
// _height parameters on every operation-mode change: 2048 docked, 1536 in
// handheld. The per-frame shadow draw then scales that size by the viewport
// ratio and takes a minimum, which only ever shrinks it. Overwriting the two
// parameter reads with immediates sidesteps both: the minimum keeps the
// immediate for any viewport at or above the reference size, and the size
// no longer depends on the dock state.
//
// The shadow map is a cascade texture array allocated per frame from the
// gsys dynamic texture pool, and 4096 is 4x the memory of the docked
// default per cascade. The stock 76 MB pool cannot hold it; install one of
// the resolution mods alongside this, which size that pool for it. Do not
// duplicate the pool offset here.

@enabled
// depth_shadow_tex_width / _height reads in the per-frame depth shadow draw.
039AF0DC 0A008252   // MOVZ W10,#4096 (was LDR W10,[X8,#0x17C0])
039AF0E0 08008252   // MOVZ W8,#4096  (was LDR W8,[X8,#0x17E0])
@stop

// Offsets reverse-engineered against Animal Crossing: New Horizons 3.0.3
// (sead + agl/gsys, NVN). The retail build is symbol-stripped; every site was
// located by structure and byte-verified against the IDB before being written.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-patches
